.TH SWIFTJXL-CLI 1 "October 8, 2026" "2.1.0-dev.2" "Swift Image Compression Suite"
.SH NAME
swiftjxl-cli \- image encoding, decoding, inspection and transcoding
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swiftjxl-cli
.RI [ options ] " command " [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
This development tool inspects headers and validates the complete supported
scalar JPEG XL frame using the public decoder. It also provides help, version
and executable capability reporting. This is not a general JPEG XL validator.
Native transcode recompresses JPEG coefficients to JPEG XL and reconstructs
the original JPEG bytes from valid reconstruction data, entirely in memory.
Build with Swift 6.2 or later in Swift 6 language mode.
Apple OS minimum is 26.0.
CLI hosts are macOS and Linux; consult qualification records for executed
coverage.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B capabilities [\-\-json]
Report executable support. Inspect and validate are available; encode and
decode accept the explicit UInt16 NRRD and integer PNM/PAM profiles.
JSON is one document on stdout.
.TP
.B help [command]
Show global or command-specific help. No arguments also show global help.
.TP
.B version
Show the development version.
.TP
.B inspect, validate
Require \-i/\-\-input PATH; a hyphen reads stdin. Inspect reports supported
headers, without checking pixel integrity. Validate decodes the entire
supported frame in memory and discards pixels. Supports unsigned
greyscale/RGB Modular with optional alpha,
8 through 16 meaningful bits, dimensions up to 1024, one frame
and compressed input at most 4 MiB. Unsupported profiles return 4.
Optional \-o/\-\-output PATH writes a report; the default is stdout.
Use \-\-json for structured output, including pixelPayloadValidated.
File reports publish atomically; \-\-overwrite permits replacement of an
existing regular file. Input aliases and output symlinks are refused.
Failure preserves any previous report; partial stdout cannot be rolled back.
.TP
.B Inspection and validation limits
Input format is jxl or jpeg-xl. Backend is automatic (default) or scalar-cpu;
accelerated is unavailable. Copy policy defaults to require-sharing;
allow-copy is accepted. Threads is a ceiling from 1 to 8; one worker is used.
Maximum memory is positive bytes, default 1073741824, including command
buffers and codec admission; it is not a process RSS ceiling.
Timeout is positive finite seconds, at most 31536000, default 120, checked
cooperatively across input, codec and output. Pipe polling checks every 25 ms;
filesystem
calls depend on operating-system scheduling. Ctrl+C returns 130.
Mode, max-error and output-format do not apply to these two commands.
.TP
.B encode, decode
Encode requires \-\-input-format; decode requires \-\-output-format.
Select nrrd, pnm or pnm-srgb explicitly.
The compressed endpoint defaults to jxl; jpeg-xl is also accepted.
Use \-i/\-\-input and optional \-o/\-\-output; a hyphen denotes a stream.
Encode and decode dimensions are at most 1024.
The explicit NRRD0005 profile is attached, raw, 2D, full-precision UInt16,
with little/big endian and x as fastest axis. Encode assigns D65/sRGB and
default intent. Decode rejects lower meaningful precision or metadata
that this profile cannot preserve. Header limits: 16384 bytes, 64 lines,
1024 bytes per line. Detached data, spatial metadata and custom keys reject.
Lossless mode is the only encode mode and default; max-error is unsupported.
Memory, worker, timeout, backend and copy-policy limits are as above.
Output is binary; JSON success reports go to stderr after publication.
Requested verbosity also uses stderr. Reporting failure cannot retract
published output. Broken binary output never emits a success report.
Encoding shares retained input bytes with the codec; decoding writes borrowed
rows directly. No extra full-image serialisation array is created.
Shell pipes still copy bytes and do not share allocations between processes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help, including after a command.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the development version.
.TP
.B \-v, \-vv, \-vvv, \-vvvv, \-vvvvv
Increase diagnostic verbosity, up to 5.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose LEVEL, \-\-verbose=LEVEL
Set level to 1 through 5, or + through +++++. Bare verbose increments once.
.TP
.B \-verbose: LEVEL, \-verbose:LEVEL
Equivalent explicit verbosity spelling; bare \-verbose increments once.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Suppress optional diagnostics; errors remain visible. Conflicts with
verbosity.
.SH DIAGNOSTIC LEVELS
Default 0 reports errors only. Levels are cumulative:
1 summary; 2 stages; 3 capability/configuration details; 4 elapsed timing;
5 bounded trace. Invalid levels or totals above 5 return 2.
Explicit levels set and repeated flags increment in argument order.
Diagnostics use stderr. Requested help/version/capability data uses stdout.
Diagnostic writes do not wait for stderr to drain. An unavailable diagnostic
stream returns I/O failure (6). Final error messages are best effort and cannot
block the original failure, deadline (5) or cancellation (130) exit status.
No payload bytes, metadata, raw addresses or input/output paths are logged.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success/help/version; 2 invalid usage; 3 malformed input;
4 unsupported feature/layout/backend/format; 5 resource/deadline;
6 input/output failure including a closed pipe; 7 internal failure;
130 user cancellation.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
swiftjxl-cli \-h
swiftjxl-cli help capabilities
swiftjxl-cli capabilities \-\-json \-vv
swiftjxl-cli capabilities \-verbose: 3
swiftjxl-cli capabilities \-\-verbose=+++++
.fi
.SH INSTALLATION
Scripts/install-cli.sh installs or updates the executable and this page
together.
Use \-\-prefix for an absolute prefix (default /usr/local), \-\-destdir or
DESTDIR
for staging, and \-\-binary for a prebuilt binary matching VERSION.
Files are PREFIX/bin/swiftjxl-cli and PREFIX/share/man/man1/swiftjxl-cli.1.
For custom prefixes use man \-M PREFIX/share/man swiftjxl-cli, or configure
MANPATH.
No index refresh is needed for direct lookup; no sudo runs automatically.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR man (1)
.PP
CLI.md and Documentation/Engineering/OS27CLI/README.md in the SwiftJXL
repository.

.SH NATIVE JPEG TRANSCODING
.B transcode --input PATH --input-format FORMAT --output-format FORMAT
supports jpeg to jxl/jpeg-xl and the reverse pair. Both formats are required.
Mode is lossless (default), preserving the original JPEG bytes. The reverse
operation needs valid reconstruction data; it never consults an original JPEG.
Supports 8-bit baseline, extended and progressive Huffman JPEG, greyscale
or three components, common 444/422/420/440 sampling, dimensions up to 2048.
CLI input and output are limited to 4 MiB. RGB/greyscale ICC profiles are
preserved. Unsupported frame profiles return 4.
Lossy/near-lossless, max-error and source-file fallback
are unavailable.
Output defaults to stdout; --output selects an atomic final file transaction.
--overwrite explicitly permits replacement. --json writes the final success
report to stderr after binary publication. Limits and stream behaviour follow
encode/decode; processing creates no intermediate image file.

.SH COLOUR INTERCHANGE
The pnm profile accepts one binary P5/P6/P7 image, greyscale or RGB,
with optional straight alpha, 8 to 16 meaningful bits and MAXVAL=2^bits-1.
Dimensions are at most 1024; input is at most 4 MiB. Multi-byte samples are
big endian. Standard colour uses BT.709 transfer. The pnm-srgb variant
requires explicit selection on both import and export; file syntax alone
cannot distinguish it. No rescaling or colour conversion occurs.
Premultiplied alpha, ICC, other interpretation metadata, unsupported tuple
meanings and extra frames reject. Headers are bounded to 16 KiB, numeric
tokens to 64 bytes, and PAM to 64 lines of at most 1024 bytes each.
After the P5/P6 MAXVAL exactly one whitespace delimiter precedes the raster;
any subsequent whitespace or hash byte is sample data.
